      "text": "The given cubic equation is $x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0$. By Vieta's formulas, the roots $r$, $s$, and $t$ satisfy:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 20,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18,\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 7.\n\\]\n\nFirst, we square the sum $r + s + t = 20$ to find $rs + rt + st$:\n\\[\n(r + s + t)^2 = r^2 + s^2 + t^2 + 2(rs + rt + st).\n\\]\nSubstituting the given value $rs + rt + st = 18$, we get\n\\[\n400 = r^2 + s^2 + t^2 + 2 \\cdot 18,\n\\]\n\\[\n400 = r^2 + s^2 + t^2 + 36,\n\\]\n\\[\nr^2 + s^2 + t^2 = 364.\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the product $rst = 7$. We aim to find $(1+r)(1+s)(1+t)$. Expanding this, we have:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + rs + rt + st + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rst.\n\\]\n\nRearrange and substitute Vieta's relations:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + 18 + 20 + 7 + rs + rt + st,\n\\]\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + 18 + 20 + 7 + 18,\n\\]\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 64.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of $(1+r)(1+s)(1+t)$ is \\boxed{64}.",
