      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the value of $(1+r)(1+s)(1+t)$, where $r$, $s$, and $t$ are the roots of the equation $x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0$. By Vieta's formulas, we know that:\n- $r + s + t = 20$ (sum of the roots),\n- $rs + rt + st = 18$ (sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time),\n- $rst = 7$ (product of the roots).\n\nLet's expand $(1+r)(1+s)(1+t)$:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rst.\n\\]\nBy substituting the known values from Vieta's formulas, we get:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46.\n\\]\nThus, the value of $(1+r)(1+s)(1+t)$ is $\\boxed{46}$.\n\nWe can verify this with Python code to ensure the result is accurate.\n```python\n# Given roots and their corresponding sums using Vieta's formulas\nr_plus_s_plus_t = 20  # sum of the roots\nrs_plus_rt_plus_st = 18  # sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time\nrst = 7  # product of the roots\n\n# Calculating the value of (1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\nresult = 1 + r_plus_s_plus_t + rs_plus_rt_plus_st + rst\nprint(result)\n```",
