      "text": "Let's start by understanding the problem and the given polynomial equation. The polynomial is \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\) and the roots are \\(r, s, t\\). From Vieta's formulas, we know:\n\\[r + s + t = 20,\\]\n\\[rs + rt + st = 18,\\]\n\\[rst = 7.\\]\nWe need to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\). We can expand \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) as follows:\n\\[(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rst.\\]\nSubstituting the known values from Vieta's formulas, we get:\n\\[1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rst = 1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46.\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{46}\\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values from Vieta's formulas for the polynomial x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\r\nr_plus_s_plus_t = 20  # sum of the roots\r\nrs_plus_rt_plus_st = 18  # sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time\r\nrst = 7  # product of the roots\r\n\r\n# Calculate (1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\r\nresult = 1 + r_plus_s_plus_t + rs_plus_rt_plus_st + rst\r\nprint(result)\n```",
